{
  "_doc": "Local speech-to-text model catalog (dot-4uzgol.66). One entry per model `stt.local.model` accepts; the runtime (whisper.cpp, sherpa-onnx or coreml) comes from here, not from config. Files are fetched from `url` (or `<stt.local.model_url>/<dir>/<name>` when a mirror is set) and must match `sha256`. `dir` empty: the single file sits directly in the models directory; otherwise the files go into <models_dir>/<dir>. `arch` picks the sherpa-onnx model config (transducer, moonshine); a coreml entry is `tdt` (FluidAudio's Parakeet pipeline: encoder, decoder and joint .mlmodelc bundles plus the vocabulary, a file name may hold one `/`-separated bundle path) with its blank token and duration bins in `tdt`. `fallback` (dot-4uzgol.69) names the entry used instead where this build has no runtime for it (coreml off macOS) or the runtime cannot load it. `benchmark` is the published average WER (percent, lower is better) and inverse real-time factor (RTFx, higher is faster) with where each number comes from; null when no published figure fits the model as shipped. RTFx from the Open ASR Leaderboard is measured on a datacentre GPU, so it ranks models but is not laptop speed. English only (dot-4uzgol.68): the multilingual parakeet v3 and whisper small/base/tiny were dropped; keys.rs STT_RETIRED_MODELS maps each to its English replacement. Keep crates/core/src/config/keys.rs STT_LOCAL_MODELS in the same order (a test checks).",
